      {
        "def_id": 68,
        "item_meta": {
          "name": [
            {
              "Ident": [
                "core",
                0
              ]
            },
            {
              "Ident": [
                "marker",
                0
              ]
            },
            {
              "Ident": [
                "PhantomData",
                0
              ]
            },
            {
              "Instantiated": {
                "params": {
                  "regions": [],
                  "types": [],
                  "const_generics": [],
                  "trait_clauses": [],
                  "regions_outlive": [],
                  "types_outlive": [],
                  "trait_type_constraints": []
                },
                "skip_binder": {
                  "regions": [],
                  "types": [
                    {
                      "Deduplicated": 798
                    }
                  ],
                  "const_generics": [],
                  "trait_refs": []
                },
                "kind": "Other"
              }
            }
          ],
          "span": {
            "data": {
              "file_id": 21,
              "beg": {
                "line": 811,
                "col": 0
              },
              "end": {
                "line": 811,
                "col": 39
              }
            },
            "generated_from_span": null
          },
          "source_text": null,
          "attr_info": {
            "attributes": [
              {
                "DocComment": " Zero-sized type used to mark things that \"act like\" they own a `T`."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " Adding a `PhantomData<T>` field to your type tells the compiler that your"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " type acts as though it stores a value of type `T`, even though it doesn't"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " really. This information is used when computing certain safety properties."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " For a more in-depth explanation of how to use `PhantomData<T>`, please see"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " [the Nomicon](../../nomicon/phantom-data.html)."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # A ghastly note \ud83d\udc7b\ud83d\udc7b\ud83d\udc7b"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " Though they both have scary names, `PhantomData` and 'phantom types' are"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " related, but not identical. A phantom type parameter is simply a type"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " parameter which is never used. In Rust, this often causes the compiler to"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " complain, and the solution is to add a \"dummy\" use by way of `PhantomData`."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # Examples"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ## Unused lifetime parameters"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " Perhaps the most common use case for `PhantomData` is a struct that has an"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " unused lifetime parameter, typically as part of some unsafe code. For"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " example, here is a struct `Slice` that has two pointers of type `*const T`,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " presumably pointing into an array somewhere:"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```compile_fail,E0392"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " struct Slice<'a, T> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     start: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     end: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " The intention is that the underlying data is only valid for the"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " lifetime `'a`, so `Slice` should not outlive `'a`. However, this"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " intent is not expressed in the code, since there are no uses of"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " the lifetime `'a` and hence it is not clear what data it applies"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " to. We can correct this by telling the compiler to act *as if* the"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " `Slice` struct contained a reference `&'a T`:"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " use std::marker::PhantomData;"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # #[allow(dead_code)]"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " struct Slice<'a, T> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     start: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     end: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     phantom: PhantomData<&'a T>,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " This also in turn infers the lifetime bound `T: 'a`, indicating"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " that any references in `T` are valid over the lifetime `'a`."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " When initializing a `Slice` you simply provide the value"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " `PhantomData` for the field `phantom`:"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # #![allow(dead_code)]"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # use std::marker::PhantomData;"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # struct Slice<'a, T> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " #     start: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " #     end: *const T,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " #     phantom: PhantomData<&'a T>,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " fn borrow_vec<T>(vec: &Vec<T>) -> Slice<'_, T> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     let ptr = vec.as_ptr();"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     Slice {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         start: ptr,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         end: unsafe { ptr.add(vec.len()) },"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         phantom: PhantomData,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ## Unused type parameters"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " It sometimes happens that you have unused type parameters which"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " indicate what type of data a struct is \"tied\" to, even though that"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " data is not actually found in the struct itself. Here is an"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " example where this arises with [FFI]. The foreign interface uses"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " handles of type `*mut ()` to refer to Rust values of different"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " types. We track the Rust type using a phantom type parameter on"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " the struct `ExternalResource` which wraps a handle."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " [FFI]: ../../book/ch19-01-unsafe-rust.html#using-extern-functions-to-call-external-code"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # #![allow(dead_code)]"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # trait ResType { }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # struct ParamType;"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # mod foreign_lib {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " #     pub fn new(_: usize) -> *mut () { 42 as *mut () }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " #     pub fn do_stuff(_: *mut (), _: usize) {}"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " # fn convert_params(_: ParamType) -> usize { 42 }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " use std::marker::PhantomData;"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " struct ExternalResource<R> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "    resource_handle: *mut (),"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "    resource_type: PhantomData<R>,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " impl<R: ResType> ExternalResource<R> {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     fn new() -> Self {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         let size_of_res = size_of::<R>();"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         Self {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "             resource_handle: foreign_lib::new(size_of_res),"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "             resource_type: PhantomData,"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     fn do_stuff(&self, param: ParamType) {"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         let foreign_params = convert_params(param);"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "         foreign_lib::do_stuff(self.resource_handle, foreign_params);"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": "     }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " }"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ```"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ## Ownership and the drop check"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " The exact interaction of `PhantomData` with drop check **may change in the future**."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " Currently, adding a field of type `PhantomData<T>` indicates that your type *owns* data of type"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " `T` in very rare circumstances. This in turn has effects on the Rust compiler's [drop check]"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " analysis. For the exact rules, see the [drop check] documentation."
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " ## Layout"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " For all `T`, the following are guaranteed:"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " * `size_of::<PhantomData<T>>() == 0`"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " * `align_of::<PhantomData<T>>() == 1`"
              },
              {
                "DocComment": ""
              },
              {
                "DocComment": " [drop check]: Drop#drop-check"
              }
            ],
            "inline": null,
            "rename": null,
            "public": true
          },
          "is_local": false,
          "opacity": "Foreign",
          "lang_item": "phantom_data"
        },
